course: dictionary
lesson: 15234
title: Shard: sharp broken pieces
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shard is a sharp, broken piece of something hard, such as glass, pottery, metal or ice. «She dropped the cup and it broke into shards on the kitchen floor.» The words sharp and broken are clues, so the shards are the broken pieces.
explain: Use context to check your meaning. Ask: what word would fit here? In the sentence, «broken piece» fits, so shard must mean a broken piece. Then swap it in: «it broke into broken pieces on the kitchen floor» still makes sense.
explain: Shard can also mean a small bit of something you cannot hold, like light or a memory. «A shard of sunlight came through the gap in the curtains.» Sunlight cannot really break, so the author is using shard in a figurative way, to show a thin, bright bit.
fact: A shard is a sharp, broken piece of glass, pottery, metal or ice.
fact: The plural of shard is shards: one shard, many shards.
fact: Archaeologists dig up pottery shards to learn how people lived long ago.
fact: Broken glass must be swept up by an adult and wrapped before it goes in the bin.
fact: The Shard is a very tall, pointed skyscraper in London, named because it looks like a piece of glass.
exercise: «The vase fell off the shelf and broke into shards.» What are the shards? | Full cups of tea | Soft cushions from the sofa | Small green leaves | *Sharp broken pieces of the vase
exercise: «Archaeologists found a pottery shard in the field.» What did they find? | A bag of sand | *A broken piece of old pottery | A bird's egg | A new plastic bottle
exercise: Jade says, «A shard of light came through the window.» What does shard mean here? | *A small, bright bit of light | A loud noise | A heavy stone wall | A sharp knife
test: Which word is the plural of shard? | *shards | shardy | shard's | sharding
test: «The ice on the pond cracked into shards.» What does shards mean here? | Long thin icicles hanging from a roof | *Sharp broken pieces of ice | Soft warm snow | Deep blue water
exam: Why must an adult sweep up broken glass shards before you go near them? | Because shards are soft and safe to touch | So the glass can be sold to a shop | *So the sharp pieces are not left lying around to cut someone | Because glass shards make good plant food
